<u>Place specific examples include:</u>

Locational details - *Cyprus is located about 80 km (50 mi) south of the coast of Turkey, in the Eastern Mediterranean Sea* Specific details of locations within the area 
Specific details of strategies - *Tourism is important to Cyprus as it provides thousands of jobs and contributes an average of 20% to the country's GDP. In 2006 the Cyprus Sustainable Tourism Initiative (CSTI) was launched to develop a sustainable approach to tourism in Cyprus through:* 
*Promoting the preservation, conservation and protection of Cyprus's environment, whilst sustainably using its natural resources. Cyprus achieved this by limiting the use of grass and exotic vegetation requiring frequent watering, reduce the number of large hotel swimming pools. Conservation of Cyprus's turtles by organising turtle watches during hatching time to ensure the hatchlings get to the sea and not into hotel resorts. Conservation of local art and history, whilst spreading benefits of tourism to poorer, rural regions through community accommodation and local events.* 
*Reduced its tourist carbon footprint by increasing the use of renewable energy at hotels and tourist complexes and working with the tourism sector to reduce demand and consumption of single use plastics in tourist hotspots such as Ayia Napa...*

